+# Perf history
+
+## SessionStart health gate
+
+Cost of the `SessionStart` health-gate hook, p50, on a 5k-record store.
+
+| When | p50 | Change bundled into the measurement |
+|---|---|---|
+| Before | 11.9 ms | `quick_check` still ran on the read path |
+| After | 1.05 ms | `quick_check` taken off the read path, `fts_rows` counter added, body `CHECK` constraint added |
+
+Notes:
+- These are measured numbers from a prior session's transcript (recorded via Muninn, trust level 1 — seen in this project's own transcripts, not independently verified here), not estimates.
+- The three changes (dropping `quick_check` from the read path, adding the `fts_rows` counter, adding the body `CHECK`) landed together, so the 11.9 ms → 1.05 ms delta is their combined effect, not attributable to any single change in isolation.
+- This checkout's git history has a single `base` commit and no stored benchmark artifacts, so the numbers above could not be independently reproduced from files currently in the repo; re-run the health-gate benchmark against a 5k-record store to reverify if needed.
